<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="he" dir="rtl">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>צ׳אט</title>
  <style>
    /* This page's own: radii, type, and the names a conversation uses — each pointed at the office's
       palette (the generated block below, kept identical to platform-base/bina-ui/theme-tokens.css by
       gate G27). What I wrote is a tint of the brand's olive; what I was sent is the surface; the
       room behind them is the page's ground. Nothing here writes a colour, so the dark ground needs
       no rule of its own. */
    :root{--radius:16px;--radius-sm:10px;--radius-pill:999px;
      --shadow-xs:0 1px 2px var(--line);--shadow-md:var(--shadow-lg);
      --bubble-out:var(--olive-soft);--bubble-out-bd:var(--olive-line);--bubble-in:var(--surface);
      --chat-bg:var(--bg);--chat-dot:color-mix(in srgb,var(--ink) 4.5%,transparent);
      --font:"Segoe UI",system-ui,-apple-system,"Noto Sans Hebrew","Assistant",Arial,sans-serif}
/* @bina-theme-tokens:start */
/* OLIVE GROVE — the one palette of the office (the owner, 2026-10-07 · DGO-450). Four hues, sampled
   from his mock-up, and the ground they stand on. A screen never writes a colour: it names one of
   these. Each hue is the colour itself (a FILL — a button, a bar, a dot), «-d» for text and thin
   lines on the ground (4.5:1 or more), «-soft» and «-line» for a tint and its hairline, and «-ink»
   for what is written ON the fill. The role names every screen already uses point at them:
   (no backtick in this block: one of its copies lives inside a script's template string)
     olive  the brand and the main action · what is well, what is done
     sky    what is in motion, what only informs · a link
     lime   look here — a warning, something waiting
     plum   a person must act — a failure, a removal, the one final action
   Contrast, measured (WCAG): ink on the ground 13.7 · muted 4.65 · light text on olive 5.51 and on
   plum 9.54 · ink on lime 6.88 · its ink on sky 6.32 · sky-d 4.61 · lime-d 4.70 · violet 5.32 ·
   on the desk: its ink 6.32 (dark: 13.96), and 11.2 where the sky pales (dark: 5.12). */
:root,:root[data-theme="light"]{
  color-scheme:light;
  accent-color:var(--accent);   /* the browser's OWN controls - a checkbox, a radio, a range, a progress bar - on both grounds: said once, here (it was said for eight single controls, and every other one was the browser's blue) */
  --bg:#f3f5f7; --surface:#fff; --surface-2:#f9fafb; --ink:#1f2a17; --muted:#6a7068; --line:#dcdfde;
  --olive:#56693f; --olive-d:#475734; --olive-soft:#e7eae4; --olive-line:#bfc6b6; --olive-ink:#f3f5f7;
  --sky:#7baae3; --sky-d:#2a6fc4; --sky-soft:#edf3fb; --sky-line:#cddff4; --sky-ink:#13263f;
  --lime:#a9b84c; --lime-d:#69732e; --lime-soft:#f3f5e6; --lime-line:#dee4bb; --lime-ink:#1f2a17;
  --plum:#5b3349; --plum-d:#4a303b; --plum-soft:#e8e2e6; --plum-line:#c1b1ba; --plum-ink:#f3f5f7;
  --accent:var(--olive); --accent-d:var(--olive-d); --accent-soft:var(--olive-soft); --accent-ink:var(--olive-ink);
  --blue:var(--sky-d); --amber:var(--lime-d); --red:var(--plum);
  --violet:#7c5c6d;   /* plum, lifted a fifth toward white: someone has to look — nothing has failed */
  --ok:var(--olive); --warn:var(--lime-d); --danger:var(--plum); --info:var(--sky-d);
  --ok-soft:var(--olive-soft); --warn-soft:var(--lime-soft); --danger-soft:var(--plum-soft); --info-soft:var(--sky-soft);
  --red-soft:var(--plum-soft); --amber-soft:var(--lime-soft); --blue-soft:var(--sky-soft); --violet-soft:var(--plum-soft);
  --side:var(--olive); --side-ink:#f3f5f7; --side-mut:#dce1da; --side-line:#788765;
  --desk:var(--sky); --desk-ink:var(--sky-ink);   /* desktop mode's ground is the sky (the owner, DGO-452), and what is written straight on it */
  --scrim:rgba(31,42,23,.5);                      /* what dims a screen behind a pop-up */
  --shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(31,42,23,.08),0 6px 24px rgba(31,42,23,.06);
  --shadow-lg:0 20px 60px rgba(31,42,23,.28);
  /* ONE COLOUR AND ONE ANIMAL PER OFFICE (the owner, 2026-10-09 · flt-002). When offices are linked,
     a person reads WHICH office a thing belongs to without opening it, so each office gets a hue of
     its own. The hue is an IDENTITY and never a health state: an office that stopped answering keeps
     its colour, and the quiet mark is the one that says "not answering". Each is an ALIAS of the
     palette's own hue — no fourth value is invented, and because the ground re-points the hue, the
     office mark follows the ground by itself. Each office's animal (elephant, deer, eagle) is a
     glyph of bina-icons.js. */
  --office-hp:var(--muted);   /* hp · elephant — grey: the heavy laptop at home, in the palette's own grey */
  --office-mac:var(--lime);   /* macbook · deer — yellow: the palette has one yellow and it is lime. A FILL, so what is written ON it is --lime-ink, never this */
  --office-vps:var(--sky-d);  /* vps · eagle — deep sky blue, «the eagle in the clouds». THE OWNER'S OWN CHOICE (2026-10-09, in writing: vps = נשר + כחול-שמיים) — this line is the colour he picked, not a default kept for him */
}

/* ── A LINKED OFFICE'S MARK, BY NAME (flt-004) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
   The link carries a NAME — mark: {color, animal} in the catalog, from the office's own identity
   — and never a value: the office that DRAWS a linked tile owns the pixels, so it paints the name
   with its own palette. These seven rules are that translation, one per family above; a screen sets
   data-office-hue="lime" and paints var(--office-hue).
   A name this file does not know paints nothing, which is why the vocabulary in
   apps/dgo-extend/identity.py may only name families that exist here — and why --red and --ok
   are not among them: they mean «danger» and «it is well» on every screen in the office. */
[data-office-hue="grey"]   { --office-hue:var(--muted); }
[data-office-hue="lime"]   { --office-hue:var(--lime); }
[data-office-hue="sky"]    { --office-hue:var(--sky-d); }
[data-office-hue="olive"]  { --office-hue:var(--olive-d); }
[data-office-hue="plum"]   { --office-hue:var(--plum); }
[data-office-hue="blue"]   { --office-hue:var(--blue); }
[data-office-hue="violet"] { --office-hue:var(--violet); }
/* the dark ground is the same four hues on the palette's own ink, and the SAME legend. Olive on that
   ink is 2.5:1, so its text step there is olive LIFTED — its own hue and saturation, lighter (7.14
   on a card, 4.82 on its own tint) — and the brand, the main action and «it is well» take that step.
   Lime stays «look here» and the sky «in motion», as on the light ground: were lime the accent here
   (it was, for a day), a warning, a selection and «it is well» were one colour. Each «-d» on its
   own «-soft» there, measured: olive 4.82 · sky 4.62 · lime 4.63 · plum 4.71. */
@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){
  :root{ color-scheme:dark;
         --bg:#141b0f; --surface:#1f2a17; --surface-2:#192213; --ink:#f3f5f7; --muted:#a2a8a2; --line:#414a3b;
         --olive-d:#a5ba8c; --olive-soft:#384629; --olive-line:#56693f;
         --sky-d:#7baae3; --sky-soft:#2e3f38; --sky-line:#4d6a8c;
         --lime-d:#a9b84c; --lime-soft:#3b4622; --lime-line:#69732e;
         --plum-d:#ad99a4; --plum-soft:#402f33; --plum-line:#7c5c6d;
         --accent:var(--olive-d); --accent-ink:var(--surface);
         --red:#ad99a4; --violet:#bdadb6; --danger:#ad99a4; --ok:var(--olive-d); --side:var(--surface);
         --desk:var(--sky-ink); --desk-ink:var(--ink); --scrim:rgba(0,0,0,.6);
         --shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.4),0 6px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.3);
         --shadow-lg:0 20px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.55); }
}
:root[data-theme="midnight"]{
  color-scheme:dark;
  --bg:#141b0f; --surface:#1f2a17; --surface-2:#192213; --ink:#f3f5f7; --muted:#a2a8a2; --line:#414a3b;
  --olive-d:#a5ba8c; --olive-soft:#384629; --olive-line:#56693f;
  --sky-d:#7baae3; --sky-soft:#2e3f38; --sky-line:#4d6a8c;
  --lime-d:#a9b84c; --lime-soft:#3b4622; --lime-line:#69732e;
  --plum-d:#ad99a4; --plum-soft:#402f33; --plum-line:#7c5c6d;
  --accent:var(--olive-d); --accent-ink:var(--surface);
  --red:#ad99a4; --violet:#bdadb6; --danger:#ad99a4; --ok:var(--olive-d); --side:var(--surface);
  --desk:var(--sky-ink); --desk-ink:var(--ink); --scrim:rgba(0,0,0,.6);
  --shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.4),0 6px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.3);
  --shadow-lg:0 20px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.55);
}
/* THE KEYBOARD'S RING - what the browser draws around the stop the keyboard is on, in the palette, wherever
   a part draws none of its own. It has no specificity at all (:where), so any rule of a part wins. Two
   screens said this for themselves; on the others nearly every stop wore the browser's ring (DGO-455).
   A field keeps the offset it has - fourteen rules draw a field's own outline and say no offset. An area
   (a scroll box, a table) takes the ring inside, where nothing clips it; a control takes it outside,
   where a filled button does not hide it. */
:where(:focus-visible){outline:2px solid var(--accent)}
:where(:focus-visible:not(a,button,summary,[role=button],input,select,textarea)){outline-offset:-2px}
:where(a,button,summary,[role=button]):focus-visible{outline-offset:2px}
/* HEBREW AT A HEAVY WEIGHT - on Windows, where the first family of --font is installed. "Segoe UI" has its
   Hebrew in Light, Regular, Semibold and Bold. Asked for 800 or 900 the browser takes the family's Black
   face, which has none, and so has every family after it - so the Hebrew of every title at 800 was drawn in
   the system's last-resort serif, thin, beside Latin in Black: «חשבונות ומראות» at 20px is 150px wide at 700
   and 120px at 800 (Chrome 154; the screens ask for 800 in 167 places, the question's title among them).
   These faces give the family's HEBREW RANGE the faces that have it. A family a sheet names is no longer the
   system's for those characters, so every weight and both styles are named, each as the system resolves it:
   measured, only upright 800 and 900 change. Any other character is not theirs and goes on to the next
   family the screen names - system-ui in --font, on Windows the same faces, Black included - which is why
   G27 asks that system-ui follows wherever a screen names this family itself. Where the family is not
   installed nothing here resolves and nothing changes. */
@font-face{font-family:"Segoe UI";src:local("Segoe UI Light");font-weight:100 300;unicode-range:U+0590-05FF,U+FB1D-FB4F}
@font-face{font-family:"Segoe UI";src:local("Segoe UI");font-weight:400;unicode-range:U+0590-05FF,U+FB1D-FB4F}
@font-face{font-family:"Segoe UI";src:local("Segoe UI Semibold");font-weight:500 600;unicode-range:U+0590-05FF,U+FB1D-FB4F}
@font-face{font-family:"Segoe UI";src:local("Segoe UI Bold");font-weight:700 900;unicode-range:U+0590-05FF,U+FB1D-FB4F}
@font-face{font-family:"Segoe UI";src:local("Segoe UI Light Italic");font-weight:100 300;font-style:italic;unicode-range:U+0590-05FF,U+FB1D-FB4F}
@font-face{font-family:"Segoe UI";src:local("Segoe UI Italic");font-weight:400;font-style:italic;unicode-range:U+0590-05FF,U+FB1D-FB4F}
@font-face{font-family:"Segoe UI";src:local("Segoe UI Semibold Italic");font-weight:500 600;font-style:italic;unicode-range:U+0590-05FF,U+FB1D-FB4F}
@font-face{font-family:"Segoe UI";src:local("Segoe UI Bold Italic");font-weight:700 900;font-style:italic;unicode-range:U+0590-05FF,U+FB1D-FB4F}
/* @bina-theme-tokens:end */
    *{box-sizing:border-box}html,body{margin:0;height:100%}
    body{background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);font-family:var(--font);font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;text-rendering:optimizeLegibility}
    .muted{color:var(--muted)}.small{font-size:12px}
    ::-webkit-scrollbar{width:9px;height:9px}::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--muted) 32%,transparent);border-radius:9px;border:2px solid transparent;background-clip:padding-box}
    ::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--muted) 50%,transparent);background-clip:padding-box}
    button{font-family:inherit}
    .tag{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;font-size:10px;font-weight:800;border-radius:999px;padding:1px 7px;letter-spacing:.01em;line-height:1.55}
    .tag-cust,.tag-bot{background:var(--info-soft);color:var(--blue)}.tag-supp{background:var(--violet-soft);color:var(--violet)}
    .tag-grp{background:var(--accent-soft);color:var(--accent-d)}

    .chat{display:flex;height:100vh;overflow:hidden;background:var(--bg)}

    /* ── sidebar ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    aside.side{width:248px;flex:none;background:var(--surface);border-inline-start:1px solid var(--line);
      display:flex;flex-direction:column;order:-1}
    aside.side .brand{padding:18px 18px 15px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:11px}
    aside.side .brand .logo{width:38px;height:38px;border-radius:11px;flex:none;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;
      background:var(--olive);color:var(--olive-ink);box-shadow:var(--shadow)}
    aside.side .brand h1{font-size:19px;font-weight:800;margin:0;letter-spacing:-.02em}
    aside.side .brand .sub{font-size:11.5px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:1px}
    .newbtn{margin:2px 14px 8px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:8px;padding:11px;border:none;border-radius:12px;
      background:var(--accent);color:var(--accent-ink);font-weight:700;font-size:13.5px;cursor:pointer;box-shadow:var(--shadow);transition:.15s}
    .newbtn:hover{background:var(--accent-d);transform:translateY(-1px);box-shadow:var(--shadow-lg)}
    .newbtn:active{transform:translateY(0)}
    .side-lbl{padding:14px 20px 6px;font-size:10.5px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.09em;color:var(--muted);text-transform:uppercase}
    .botctl{margin:2px 14px 6px;padding:14px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;background:linear-gradient(180deg,var(--surface),var(--surface-2));box-shadow:var(--shadow-xs)}
    .botctl .h{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:800;color:var(--ink)}
    .botctl .h .bi{width:26px;height:26px;border-radius:8px;background:var(--accent-soft);color:var(--accent-d);display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;flex:none}
    .selwrap{position:relative;margin-top:11px}
    /* the select's chevron is DRAWN (two borders of a turned square), not a character of the font — and it
       stands at the END of the line, where the select keeps room for it: at the start it lay over the first
       letter of the option («בוט» read «צוט») */
    .selwrap::after{content:"";position:absolute;inset-inline-end:13px;top:50%;width:6px;height:6px;border:solid var(--muted);border-width:0 1.6px 1.6px 0;transform:translateY(-70%) rotate(45deg);pointer-events:none}
    .botctl select{width:100%;padding:9px 12px;padding-inline-end:30px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;font:inherit;font-size:13px;font-weight:600;
      background:var(--surface);color:var(--ink);appearance:none;cursor:pointer}
    .botctl select:focus{outline:2px solid var(--accent);border-color:transparent}
    .botctl .bd{margin-top:9px;font-size:11.5px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.5}
    .side-sp{flex:1}
    /* the account bar's own rules live with the switcher, further down — it is one control and it
       reads better in one place than split between the sim's old block and its replacement */

    /* ── conversation list ───────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .conv-col{width:352px;flex:none;background:var(--surface);border-inline-start:1px solid var(--line);display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-width:0}
    .conv-head{padding:16px 18px 10px}
    .conv-head .r{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between}
    .conv-head h2{margin:0;font-size:19px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.02em}
    .conv-head .cnt{font-size:11px;font-weight:800;color:var(--muted);background:var(--bg);border-radius:999px;padding:2px 9px}
    .search{position:relative;margin-top:12px}
    .search input{width:100%;padding:10px 38px 10px 14px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;font:inherit;font-size:13px;background:var(--surface-2);color:var(--ink);transition:.15s}
    .search input:focus{outline:none;border-color:var(--accent);background:var(--surface);box-shadow:0 0 0 3px var(--accent-soft)}
    .search svg{position:absolute;inset-inline-start:12px;top:50%;transform:translateY(-50%);color:var(--muted)}
    .segtabs{display:flex;gap:3px;padding:3px;margin:12px 18px 4px;background:var(--bg);border-radius:11px}
    .seg{flex:1;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:5px;padding:7px 6px;border-radius:8px;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;color:var(--muted);cursor:pointer;transition:.15s;border:none;background:transparent}
    .seg:hover{color:var(--ink)}
    .seg.on{background:var(--surface);color:var(--accent-d);box-shadow:var(--shadow-xs)}
    .seg .n{font-size:10px;font-weight:800;background:var(--bg);color:var(--muted);border-radius:999px;padding:0 6px;min-width:16px;text-align:center}
    /* a count is said once it is KNOWN: the four stood «0» in the markup, beside a chat that could not be read */
    .conv-head .cnt:empty,.seg .n:empty{display:none}
    .seg.on .n{background:var(--accent-soft);color:var(--accent-d)}
    .conv-list{flex:1;min-height:0;overflow-y:auto;padding:4px 10px 14px}
    .conv{display:flex;gap:12px;padding:10px 11px;border-radius:14px;cursor:pointer;align-items:center;position:relative;transition:background .12s}
    .conv:hover{background:var(--surface-2)}
    .conv.on{background:var(--accent-soft)}
    .conv.on::before{content:"";position:absolute;inset-inline-start:0;top:14px;bottom:14px;width:3px;border-radius:3px;background:var(--accent)}
    .avatar{position:relative;flex:none}
    .av{width:48px;height:48px;border-radius:50%;color:var(--surface);font-weight:700;font-size:16px;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;letter-spacing:.02em}
    .av.sm{width:42px;height:42px;font-size:14px}
    .presence{position:absolute;inset-inline-end:1px;bottom:1px;width:12px;height:12px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ok);border:2.5px solid var(--surface)}
    .conv.on .presence{border-color:var(--accent-soft)}
    .conv .cx{flex:1;min-width:0}
    .conv .r1{display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:8px}
    .conv .nm{font-weight:700;font-size:14.5px;color:var(--ink);white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;flex:1;min-width:0;letter-spacing:-.01em}
    .conv .tm{font-size:11px;color:var(--muted);flex:none;font-weight:600}
    .conv.unread .tm{color:var(--accent-d);font-weight:800}
    .conv .r2{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;margin-top:3px}
    .conv .lm{flex:1;min-width:0;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:4px}
    .conv.unread .lm{color:var(--ink);font-weight:600}
    .conv .lm .tick{color:var(--blue);font-weight:700;flex:none}.conv .lm .tick.gray{color:var(--muted)}
    .conv .badge{flex:none;min-width:20px;height:20px;padding:0 6px;border-radius:999px;background:var(--accent);color:var(--accent-ink);font-size:11px;font-weight:800;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;box-shadow:var(--shadow-xs)}
    .conv .pin{color:var(--muted);flex:none}
    .list-empty{padding:44px 22px;text-align:center;color:var(--muted);font-size:13px}
    .list-err{padding:40px 26px;text-align:center;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:10px}
    .list-err .le-ic{width:66px;height:66px;border-radius:20px;background:var(--danger-soft);border:1px solid var(--plum-line);color:var(--red);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center}
    .list-err b{font-size:16px;color:var(--ink);font-weight:800}
    .list-err span{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.5;max-width:280px}
    .list-err .le-btn{margin-top:4px;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;padding:11px 18px;border:none;border-radius:11px;background:var(--plum);color:var(--plum-ink);font:inherit;font-weight:700;cursor:pointer;box-shadow:var(--shadow)}

    /* ── thread ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .thread-col{flex:1;min-width:0;min-height:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:var(--chat-bg);position:relative}
    .thread-col::before{content:"";position:absolute;inset:0;pointer-events:none;opacity:1;
      background-image:radial-gradient(var(--chat-dot) 1.4px,transparent 1.4px);background-size:22px 22px;background-position:0 0}
    /* #thread must itself fill the column and establish the flex context, or the header/messages/composer
       grow past the viewport (composer disappears) and .msgs never scrolls. min-height:0 lets .msgs shrink. */
    #thread{flex:1;min-height:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column}
    .th-head,.msgs,.composer,.th-empty{position:relative;z-index:1}
    .th-head{flex:none;background:var(--surface);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:11px 20px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:13px;box-shadow:var(--shadow-xs)}
    .th-head .cx{flex:1;min-width:0}
    .th-head .nm{font-weight:800;font-size:15.5px;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;letter-spacing:-.01em}
    .th-head .hn{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;margin-top:1px}
    .th-head .hn.online{color:var(--accent-d);font-weight:600}
    .th-head .ha{display:flex;gap:2px}
    .th-head .ha button{background:transparent;border:none;color:var(--muted);cursor:pointer;padding:9px;border-radius:10px;transition:.12s;display:inline-flex}
    .th-head .ha button:hover{background:var(--surface-2);color:var(--ink)}
    .msgs{flex:1 1 auto;min-height:0;overflow-y:auto;overflow-x:hidden;overscroll-behavior:contain;padding:20px clamp(18px,4%,52px) 16px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;align-items:stretch}
    .daysep{align-self:center;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--surface) 85%,transparent);backdrop-filter:blur(4px);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:999px;
      padding:4px 14px;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--muted);margin:12px 0 8px;box-shadow:var(--shadow-xs)}
    /* bubble: fit content but never so narrow the time wraps — the time is absolutely placed in the
       bottom corner and the text reserves room for it via a trailing inline spacer (WhatsApp technique). */
    .msg{position:relative;max-width:min(64%,560px);min-width:58px;padding:6px 11px 7px;border-radius:12px;font-size:13.6px;line-height:1.4;
      box-shadow:var(--shadow-xs);margin-top:2px;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:break-word;word-break:break-word}
    .msg.in{align-self:flex-start;background:var(--bubble-in)}
    .msg.out{align-self:flex-end;background:var(--bubble-out);border:1px solid var(--bubble-out-bd)}
    .msg.head{margin-top:9px}
    .msg.in.head{border-start-start-radius:4px}
    .msg.out.head{border-start-end-radius:4px}
    .msg.in.head::before{content:"";position:absolute;top:0;inset-inline-start:-6px;width:11px;height:13px;background:var(--bubble-in);clip-path:polygon(100% 0,100% 100%,0 0)}
    .msg.out.head::before{content:"";position:absolute;top:0;inset-inline-end:-7px;width:12px;height:13px;background:var(--bubble-out);border-top:1px solid var(--bubble-out-bd);border-inline-end:1px solid var(--bubble-out-bd);clip-path:polygon(0 0,0 100%,100% 0)}
    .msg .sndr{display:block;font-size:12px;font-weight:800;margin-bottom:2px;letter-spacing:-.01em}
    .msg .txt::after{content:"";display:inline-block;width:46px;height:1px}
    .msg.out .txt::after{width:62px}
    /* An attachment chip. Sits inside the bubble, inherits its direction, and is a real anchor so
       the browser's own download handling applies. */
    .msg .att{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;margin-top:4px;padding:8px 10px;border-radius:10px;
      background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--ink) 5%,transparent);text-decoration:none;color:inherit;max-width:min(320px,70vw)}
    .msg.out .att{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--surface) 35%,transparent)}
    .msg .att:hover{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--ink) 9%,transparent)}
    .msg.out .att:hover{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--surface) 50%,transparent)}
    .msg .att-ic{font-size:18px;line-height:1;flex:0 0 auto}
    .msg .att-nm{flex:1 1 auto;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;white-space:nowrap;font-size:13px}
    .msg .att-sz{flex:0 0 auto;font-size:11px;opacity:.65}
    .msg .mt{position:absolute;inset-inline-end:11px;bottom:6px;font-size:10px;color:var(--muted);font-weight:600;line-height:1;white-space:nowrap;pointer-events:none}
    .msg.out .mt{color:var(--olive-d)}
    .msg .mt .tick{color:var(--blue);font-weight:800;margin-inline-start:1px}
    .msg .mt .tick.gray{color:var(--muted)}
    /* typing indicator */
    .typing{align-self:flex-start;background:var(--bubble-in);border-radius:14px;border-start-start-radius:5px;padding:11px 14px;box-shadow:var(--shadow-xs);display:inline-flex;gap:4px;margin-top:6px}
    .typing i{width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--muted);display:inline-block;animation:tp 1.2s infinite ease-in-out}
    .typing i:nth-child(2){animation-delay:.18s}.typing i:nth-child(3){animation-delay:.36s}
    @keyframes tp{0%,60%,100%{transform:translateY(0);opacity:.5}30%{transform:translateY(-4px);opacity:1}}
    .botnote{align-self:center;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--surface) 72%,transparent);backdrop-filter:blur(4px);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:999px;padding:4px 13px;font-size:11px;font-weight:600;color:var(--muted);margin:10px 0 4px;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px}

    .th-empty{flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:14px;color:var(--muted);text-align:center;padding:30px}
    .th-empty .big{width:96px;height:96px;border-radius:28px;background:linear-gradient(180deg,var(--surface),var(--surface-2));color:var(--accent-d);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;box-shadow:var(--shadow-md);border:1px solid var(--line)}
    .th-empty .big.err{background:var(--danger-soft);border-color:var(--plum-line);color:var(--red)}
    .th-empty h3{margin:0;font-size:18px;color:var(--ink);font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.01em}
    .th-empty p{margin:0;max-width:330px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6}

    /* ── composer ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .composer{flex:none;background:var(--surface);border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:12px 18px;display:flex;align-items:flex-end;gap:10px}
    .composer .ico{background:transparent;border:none;color:var(--muted);cursor:pointer;padding:9px;border-radius:10px;flex:none;transition:.12s;display:inline-flex}
    .composer .ico:hover{background:var(--surface-2);color:var(--accent-d)}
    .composer .field{flex:1;background:var(--surface-2);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:22px;display:flex;align-items:flex-end;padding:2px 6px 2px 4px;transition:.15s}
    .composer .field:focus-within{border-color:var(--accent);background:var(--surface);box-shadow:0 0 0 3px var(--accent-soft)}
    .composer textarea{flex:1;resize:none;max-height:120px;min-height:22px;border:none;background:transparent;padding:9px 11px;font:inherit;font-size:14px;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.4;outline:none}
    .composer .send{flex:none;width:44px;height:44px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent);color:var(--accent-ink);border:none;cursor:pointer;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;box-shadow:var(--shadow);transition:.15s}
    .composer .send:hover{background:var(--accent-d);transform:scale(1.05)}
    .composer .send:active{transform:scale(.96)}

    /* thread back button (mobile only) */
    .th-back{display:none;background:transparent;border:none;color:var(--ink);cursor:pointer;padding:6px;margin-inline-end:2px;border-radius:9px}
    .th-back:hover{background:var(--surface-2)}

    /* ── mobile-first: collapse the 3-pane layout to a single column (list → thread → back).
       Desktop (>820px) is completely untouched. Super-app pattern: full-screen sub-views. ── */
    @media (max-width:820px){
      aside.side{display:none}
      .conv-col{width:100%;flex:1 1 auto;border:none}
      .conv-head{padding:14px 16px 8px}
      .thread-col{display:none}
      .chat.mob-thread .conv-col{display:none}
      .chat.mob-thread .thread-col{display:flex;flex:1 1 auto}
      .th-back{display:inline-flex}
      .msgs{padding:16px 12px 14px}
      .msg{max-width:82%}
      .conv{padding:12px 10px}          /* taller rows for touch */
      .composer{padding:10px 12px calc(10px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom))}
      .th-head{padding:10px 12px}
      .th-head .ha button{padding:10px}  /* 44px touch targets */
    }

    /* ── account bar · the SAME control drive and mail carry ──────────────────
       Copied from apps/drive/static/index.html and apps/mail/mailapi/static/index.html rather than
       invented a third time. Their shape, exactly: `.acct` is the LAST thing in the sidebar, marked
       off by a border-top and nothing else; the button is dot + name + identity + chevron; the menu
       is absolutely positioned and opens UPWARD (`bottom:100%`) so it can never clip against the
       viewport edge, and it shrinks with its column.

       WHAT THIS REPLACED, and why it had to go. The sim's `.connftr` — a bordered row under a
       «חיבור פעיל» heading with a 30px protocol tile and `cursor:default` — was ported faithfully
       and was the wrong thing to port. It reads as a STATUS PLAQUE, so nobody discovers that it
       opens anything, and «חיבור חשבון» (which has been inside its menu all along) may as well not
       exist. Drive and mail already solved this; chat now says it the same way.

       The sim's class names are KEPT on the elements that survived — `.connftr` on the button,
       `.provico`/`.pdot` on the badge and the dot, `.cx`/`.cn`/`.cs` on the text — because the
       parity harness compares CLASS TOKENS between the sim's tree and this one. The component is the
       same component; only its treatment changed. Dropping the tokens would report five components
       as un-ported work when they had merely been restyled. */
    .acct{position:relative;border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin:4px 14px 14px;padding-top:10px;min-width:0}
    .acct-btn{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;width:100%;min-width:0;background:var(--surface-2);
      border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;padding:7px 10px;font:inherit;font-size:12.5px;
      color:var(--ink);text-align:start;cursor:pointer;transition:.15s}
    .acct-btn:hover{border-color:var(--accent)}
    .acct .dot{width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;flex:none}
    /* the protocol badge — the one part chat has that drive and mail do not, because three genuinely
       different transports answer here and "which one am I on" is not answerable from the label
       alone. Deliberately small: a piece of information, not the plaque it used to be. */
    .acct .provico{width:19px;height:19px;border-radius:6px;flex:none;display:inline-flex;
      align-items:center;justify-content:center;color:var(--olive-ink);font-size:10px;font-weight:800;line-height:1}   /* a provider's letter on the provider's colour */
    .acct-tx{flex:1;min-width:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1px}
    .acct-lbl{display:block;font-weight:700;min-width:0;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;white-space:nowrap}
    /* (a line with no letter of its own — a phone number — reads left to right: «050-000-0007» stood «50-123-4567 972+») */
    .acct-hint{display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:11px;min-width:0;overflow:hidden;
      text-overflow:ellipsis;white-space:nowrap;unicode-bidi:plaintext;text-align:right}
    .acct-chev{flex:none;color:var(--muted);font-size:10px;margin-inline-start:auto;line-height:1}
    .acct-menu{position:absolute;bottom:calc(100% + 6px);inset-inline-start:0;
      width:max(100%,244px);max-width:min(320px,86vw);background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius:12px;box-shadow:var(--shadow-md);padding:6px;z-index:60;max-height:60vh;overflow-y:auto}
    .acct-menu.hidden{display:none}
    .acct-item{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;border-radius:8px;min-width:0}
    .acct-item:hover{background:var(--accent-soft)}
    .acct-pick{flex:1;min-width:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:transparent;border:none;
      padding:8px 10px;border-radius:8px;cursor:pointer;text-align:start;color:inherit;font:inherit}
    .acct-l1{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;min-width:0}
    .acct-l1 .acct-lbl{font-size:12.5px}
    .acct-dot{width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;flex:none}
    .acct-proto{display:block;font-size:10.5px;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
    .acct-menu .acct-hint{font-size:10.5px}
    .acct-on{margin-inline-start:auto;color:var(--accent-d);font-weight:800;flex:none;font-size:12px}
    .acct-sep{height:1px;background:var(--line);margin:6px 4px}
    .acct-rm{flex:none;background:transparent;border:none;color:var(--muted);font:inherit;font-size:16px;line-height:1;
      padding:6px 8px;border-radius:9px;cursor:pointer}
    .acct-rm:hover{background:var(--danger-soft);color:var(--red)}
    .acct-rm:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--red);outline-offset:1px}
    /* ── tools · the admin dashboard's remaining jobs, in the app ──────────────
       Same parts as every other modal here (bcard / mlbl / bset-* / note / btn); the only new one is
       the subscriber table, which has no equivalent anywhere else in this UI. */
    .utab{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12.5px;margin-top:4px}
    .utab th{text-align:start;font-size:10.5px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.06em;color:var(--muted);
      text-transform:uppercase;padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);white-space:nowrap}
    .utab td{padding:7px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);color:var(--ink);
      max-width:190px;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;white-space:nowrap}
    .utab td.ltr{direction:ltr;text-align:end;unicode-bidi:plaintext;color:var(--muted)}
    .utab tr:last-child td{border-bottom:none}
    .uwrap{max-height:210px;overflow:auto;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:11px;margin-top:8px}
    .danger{border-color:var(--plum-line);color:var(--red)}
    .danger:hover{border-color:var(--red);background:var(--danger-soft)}
    .tool-sec{margin-top:16px}
    .tool-sec:first-child{margin-top:0}
    /* Mail's two-line entry, taken with its reason: three entries that do three different things
       were not telling themselves apart by title alone (an operator opened «חיבור חשבון» looking for
       "add a user" and concluded the product could not do it). The second line says what each does,
       and — as in mail — the CREATE action is named as an action and put first. */
    .acct-add{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:7px;width:100%;background:transparent;border:none;
      color:var(--accent-d);font:inherit;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;padding:9px 10px;border-radius:8px;
      cursor:pointer;text-align:start}
    .acct-add:hover{background:var(--accent-soft)}
    .acct-add:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:-2px}
    .acct-add .ai{flex:none;line-height:1.35}
    .acct-add-t{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;min-width:0;text-align:start}
    .acct-add-s{font-weight:500;font-size:11px;color:var(--muted);white-space:normal;line-height:1.35}
    .acct-warn{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:6px;color:var(--amber);font-size:11px;font-weight:600;padding:7px 5px 2px;line-height:1.45;min-width:0}
    .acct-empty{padding:10px;font-size:11.5px;color:var(--muted)}
    .mconn{display:none;align-items:center;gap:6px;margin-inline-start:auto;max-width:52%;
      background:var(--surface-2);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:999px;color:var(--ink);
      font:inherit;font-size:11.5px;font-weight:700;padding:5px 11px;cursor:pointer;
      white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
    .mconn .mdot{width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;flex:none;background:var(--ok)}
    /* AFTER the base rule, not inside the layout media query further up: same specificity, so the
       later declaration wins — putting the override earlier left the chip hidden on every phone. */
    @media (max-width:820px){.mconn{display:inline-flex}}
    /* (34px under a finger, 28 of them in the row: the head keeps its height, and the list under it its own) */
    .mnew{display:none;flex:none;align-items:center;justify-content:center;width:34px;height:34px;margin-block:-3px;margin-inline-start:8px;
      border:none;border-radius:999px;background:var(--accent);color:var(--accent-ink);cursor:pointer}
    @media (max-width:820px){.mnew{display:inline-flex}}
    .gear{background:transparent;border:none;color:var(--muted);cursor:pointer;padding:4px;border-radius:8px;
      margin-inline-start:auto;display:inline-flex;flex:none}
    .gear:hover{background:var(--bg);color:var(--accent-d)}

    /* ── modal (bot management · connect) ─────────────────────────────────────── */
    .ov{position:fixed;inset:0;background:var(--scrim);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;z-index:90;padding:20px}
    .ov.hidden{display:none}
    .modal{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:18px;box-shadow:var(--shadow-lg);
      width:min(580px,100%);max-height:86vh;display:flex;flex-direction:column}
    .modal .mh{padding:15px 20px 12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px}
    .modal .mh h3{margin:0;font-size:16.5px;font-weight:800;flex:1;letter-spacing:-.02em}
    /* `flex:1;min-height:0` is what makes overflow-y:auto actually DO anything here.
       .modal is a flex column clamped to max-height:86vh. A flex item defaults to min-height:auto,
       which refuses to shrink below its content — so .mb's own height always equalled its content
       height, there was never any overflow for it to scroll, and anything past 86vh was simply
       unreachable. On a 735px-tall window that hid the whole "add user" form of the private-engine
       screen: the modal looked complete, the footer sat where a footer should, and the wheel did
       nothing. Only keyboard focus reached the fields, because scrollIntoView moves an ancestor
       regardless of whether a scrollbar was offered. */
    .modal .mb{padding:15px 20px;flex:1;min-height:0;overflow-y:auto;overscroll-behavior:contain;font-size:13px}
    .modal .mf{padding:12px 20px 15px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);display:flex;gap:8px}
    .btn{border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--surface-2);color:var(--ink);font:inherit;font-size:13px;
      font-weight:700;padding:9px 16px;border-radius:11px;cursor:pointer;transition:.14s}
    .btn:hover{border-color:var(--accent)}
    .btn.pri{background:var(--accent);border-color:transparent;color:var(--accent-ink)}
    .btn.pri:hover{background:var(--accent-d)}
    .xbtn{background:transparent;border:none;color:var(--muted);cursor:pointer;display:inline-flex;padding:5px 8px;border-radius:8px}
    .xbtn:hover{background:var(--surface-2);color:var(--ink)}
    .mlbl{font-size:10.5px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.08em;color:var(--muted);text-transform:uppercase;margin:2px 0 6px}
    .brow{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
    .brow:last-of-type{border-bottom:none}
    .brow .bx{flex:1;min-width:0}
    .brow .bn{display:block;font-weight:700;font-size:13px;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
    .brow .bs{display:block;font-size:11px;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
    .brow select{padding:7px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;font:inherit;font-size:12.5px;
      font-weight:600;background:var(--surface);color:var(--ink);max-width:190px;cursor:pointer}
    .bcard{margin-top:14px;padding:13px 14px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:13px;background:var(--surface-2)}
    .bcard h4{margin:0 0 5px;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:800}
    .bcard p{margin:0 0 10px;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.55}
    .caps{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px}
    .cap{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:5px;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;border-radius:999px;
      padding:3px 9px;background:var(--bg);color:var(--muted)}
    .cap.on{background:var(--accent-soft);color:var(--accent-d)}
    .note{margin-top:13px;font-size:11.5px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6}

    /* ── the bot's own settings, per connection ────────────────────────────────
       A section of the bot card, not a second screen: same .bcard / .mlbl / .note / .btn parts as
       everything else in this modal. The matrix row the operator picked is highlighted with the same
       accent-soft the connection list uses for "this one", so "which row am I editing" is the same
       visual answer everywhere in the app. */
    .brow{border-radius:11px;padding-inline:8px;margin-inline:-8px;cursor:pointer}
    .brow.on{background:var(--accent-soft)}
    .brow:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:1px}
    .bset-row{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:12px;padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
    .bset-row:last-child{border-bottom:none}
    .bset-x{flex:1;min-width:0}
    .bset-lbl{display:block;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}
    .bset-hint{display:block;font-size:11px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.5;margin-top:2px}
    .bset-ctl{flex:none;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-end;gap:3px;max-width:44%}
    .bset-row input[type=number],.bset-row input[type=text],.bset-row select{
      padding:7px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;font:inherit;font-size:12.5px;
      font-weight:600;background:var(--surface);color:var(--ink);max-width:190px}
    .bset-row input[type=number]{width:104px;text-align:start}
    .bset-row input[type=text]{width:190px}
    .bset-row input:focus,.bset-row select:focus{outline:none;border-color:var(--accent);box-shadow:0 0 0 3px var(--accent-soft)}
    .bset-unit{font-size:10.5px;color:var(--muted);direction:ltr}
    .bset-row.bad input,.bset-row.bad select{border-color:var(--red);box-shadow:0 0 0 3px var(--danger-soft)}
    .bset-err{font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--red);line-height:1.45;text-align:end;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:plaintext}
    /* boolean = a switch. RTL: the knob rests at the inline-start (right) edge and slides to the left
       when on, so "on" is the same direction the rest of the RTL UI moves. */
    .sw{position:relative;display:inline-flex;flex:none;width:40px;height:23px;cursor:pointer}
    .sw input{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;opacity:0;margin:0;cursor:pointer}
    .sw i{flex:1;border-radius:999px;background:var(--bg);border:1px solid var(--line);transition:.16s;pointer-events:none}
    .sw i::after{content:"";position:absolute;top:3px;inset-inline-start:3px;width:17px;height:17px;border-radius:50%;
      background:var(--surface);box-shadow:var(--shadow-xs);transition:.16s}
    .sw input:checked+i{background:var(--accent);border-color:transparent}
    .sw input:checked+i::after{transform:translateX(-17px)}
    .sw input:focus-visible+i{outline:2px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:2px}
    .bset-foot{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;margin-top:13px;flex-wrap:wrap}
    .bset-foot .btn{padding:8px 15px;font-size:12.5px}
    .bset-state{font-size:11.5px;color:var(--muted)}
    .bset-state.bad{color:var(--red);font-weight:700}
    .prow{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:11px;padding:11px 12px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:8px}
    /* standalone, NOT `.prow .pic`: the same badge is used in the bot matrix, and `.provico` — the
       account bar's protocol badge — is scoped to `.acct`, so reusing THAT class out here produced an
       unstyled grey box. This one carries its own rule and works wherever it is put. */
    .pic{width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:10px;flex:none;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;color:var(--olive-ink);font-size:14px;font-weight:800}
    .brow .pic{width:30px;height:30px;border-radius:9px;font-size:13px}
    .prow .px{flex:1;min-width:0}
    .prow .pn{display:block;font-weight:700;font-size:13px}
    .prow .pd{display:block;font-size:11.5px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.5;margin-top:2px}

    /* ── new conversation · the people picker ─────────────────────────────────
       No new visual language: the rows are the bot matrix's .brow with the conversation list's
       .avatar/.av/.presence inside them, held in the same .uwrap scroll frame the subscriber table
       uses, and the mode switch is the conversation list's own .segtabs. The only genuinely new
       parts are the two below — a disabled state for the sidebar button, and the multi-select tick —
       because neither exists anywhere else in this app.

       The disabled state is the point of the whole screen: `listUsers`/`createDirect` are OPTIONAL
       ops, so on WhatsApp and Telegram the button would have nothing to open. It says so instead of
       opening a picker that can only 501. */
    .newbtn.off{background:var(--bg);color:var(--muted);box-shadow:none;cursor:default}
    .newbtn.off:hover{background:var(--bg);transform:none;box-shadow:none}
    .newhint{margin:-2px 14px 10px}
    .uwrap.nclist{max-height:284px;padding:0 11px}
    .uwrap.nclist .brow{margin-inline:0;padding-inline:3px}
    .uwrap.nclist .brow:last-child{border-bottom:none}
    .nc-check{flex:none;color:var(--accent-d);font-weight:800;font-size:13px;visibility:hidden}
    .brow.on .nc-check{visibility:visible}
    .mb .segtabs{margin:0 0 12px}

    /* ── the private engine's own users ───────────────────────────────────────
       No new visual language: the rows are the people picker's .brow inside the same .uwrap frame,
       with the bot settings' own .sw switch on the end and the bot card's .cap as the operator
       badge. The only genuinely new rule is the cursor — these rows are NOT a picker (the switch is
       the control), and .brow is `cursor:pointer` everywhere else in this modal. */
    .uwrap.englist{max-height:262px;padding:0 11px}
    .uwrap.englist .brow{margin-inline:0;padding-inline:3px;cursor:default}
    .uwrap.englist .brow:last-child{border-bottom:none}
    .uwrap.englist .cap{flex:none}
    /* Declared LAST so it beats the display of whatever it is put on (.bset-row is flex, and an
       equal-specificity rule earlier in the file would otherwise win). */
    .hidden{display:none}

    /* the office's notice sits above the connection chip at the foot of the side column: its usual corner IS
       that chip — the button a refused switch sends a person back to */
    body #bina-tell{inset-block-end:76px}
    /* a MARK of the page (`mark()` below): drawn at the size of the text it sits in */
    .mk{width:1em;height:1em;flex:none;vertical-align:-.14em}
    .tick{display:inline-flex}
    .tick.read .mk{stroke-width:3.2}   /* read is also HEAVIER than delivered — not told by colour alone */
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="chat">
    <aside class="side">
      <div class="brand">
        <span class="logo"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="21" height="21" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.1" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M21 11.5a8.38 8.38 0 0 1-.9 3.8 8.5 8.5 0 0 1-7.6 4.7 8.38 8.38 0 0 1-3.8-.9L3 21l1.9-5.7a8.38 8.38 0 0 1-.9-3.8 8.5 8.5 0 0 1 4.7-7.6 8.38 8.38 0 0 1 3.8-.9h.5a8.48 8.48 0 0 1 8 8v.5z"/></svg></span>
        <div><h1>צ׳אט</h1><div class="sub">שיחות מרובות ספקים</div></div>
      </div>
      <button class="newbtn" id="newChat"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="17" height="17" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>שיחה חדשה</button>
      <!-- Only rendered when the ACTIVE connection cannot start one (the ops are optional). Empty
           and display:none otherwise, so the sidebar is unchanged where the button works. -->
      <div class="note newhint hidden" id="newHint"></div>

      <!-- (hidden until an account is read: renderBotCard shows them) -->
      <div class="side-lbl" hidden>אוטומציה</div>
      <div class="botctl" hidden>
        <div class="h"><span class="bi"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="15" height="15" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="10" rx="2"/><circle cx="12" cy="5" r="2"/><path d="M12 7v4M8 16h.01M16 16h.01"/></svg></span>בוט פעיל בחיבור זה<button class="gear" id="botCfg" type="button" title="ניהול בוטים וחיבורים"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="15" height="15" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/><path d="M19.4 15a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 .33 1.82l.06.06a2 2 0 1 1-2.83 2.83l-.06-.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.82-.33 1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1 1.51V21a2 2 0 1 1-4 0v-.09A1.65 1.65 0 0 0 9 19.4a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.82.33l-.06.06a2 2 0 1 1-2.83-2.83l.06-.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 .33-1.82 1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.51-1H3a2 2 0 1 1 0-4h.09A1.65 1.65 0 0 0 4.6 9a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-.33-1.82l-.06-.06a2 2 0 1 1 2.83-2.83l.06.06A1.65 1.65 0 0 0 9 4.6a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1-1.51V3a2 2 0 1 1 4 0v.09a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1 1.51 1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1.82-.33l.06-.06a2 2 0 1 1 2.83 2.83l-.06.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-.33 1.82V9a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1.51 1H21a2 2 0 1 1 0 4h-.09a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.51 1z"/></svg></button></div>
        <div class="selwrap"><select id="botSelect"></select></div>
        <div class="bd" id="botDesc"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="side-sp"></div>
      <!-- Drive's and mail's account bar, part for part: sidebar footer, border-top, no heading of
           its own (the «חיבור פעיל» label above it was the sim's, and a label is what made this read
           as a plaque instead of a control). #acctBtn / #acctMenu are their ids too. -->
      <div class="acct" id="acct">
        <button class="acct-btn connftr" id="acctBtn" type="button" aria-haspopup="menu" aria-expanded="false"
                title="החיבור הפעיל · החלפת חיבור או חיבור חשבון">
          <span class="dot pdot" id="provDot"></span>
          <span class="provico" id="provIco">·</span>
          <span class="acct-tx cx">
            <bdi class="acct-lbl cn" id="connName">—</bdi>
            <small class="acct-hint cs muted" id="connState">טוען…</small>
          </span>
          <span class="acct-chev"><svg class="mk" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></span>
        </button>
        <div class="acct-menu hidden" id="acctMenu" role="menu"></div>
